# CI Watch

Invoke `.mt-agent-devkit/scripts/wait_work.py ci` with the selected provider,
concrete runtime binding, unique wait ID, mode, repository and PR or full SHA.
The ID binds the first inspected head; repeat the same command to resume.
Use `--required-check <name>` for each additional expected workflow/check not
declared in branch protection. A commit input has no PR protection context:
supply all expected check/workflow names and do not use it as a PR merge verdict.

```text
python .mt-agent-devkit/scripts/wait_work.py ci --provider codex --runtime-root .codex/agents --id ST-000217-review --mode github --repo owner/repo --pr 123 --window 45
```

Use receipt/state-path bindings; the example is a target layout, while devkit
internal Codex uses `.codex/agents/working`. Bash and PowerShell launchers
`wait_work.sh` and `wait_work.ps1` forward the same arguments. Python 3.10+ and
authenticated `gh` are prerequisites; never install or alter credentials merely
to make a missing capability appear supported.

| Outcome / exit | Action |
|---|---|
| PASS / 0 | All visible runs/checks and declared required names passed. Recheck current head, approval scope, and the canonical review/merge gates. This is evidence, never permission to merge. |
| FAIL / 1 | Required or conservatively included evidence failed, cancelled or timed out; route to fixes. |
| PENDING / 124 | Window expired, work/checks still pending or expected names absent. Repeat same wait ID; no gate advances. |
| NO RUN / 2 | No evidence after discovery window. Apply the existing explicit zero-check gate; never infer success. |
| ERROR / 3 | Recover missing identity/binding, CLI/authentication/network or unsupported evidence; retry same ID after recovery. |
| STALE / 4 | Head changed; old evidence cannot approve the new head. Start a new wait ID after renewed scope review. |

JSON includes inspected SHA, run IDs, check count, missing names and identity.
Prior-run candidates include their SHA, verdict and changed-file comparison, but
remain NO RUN. Confirm suppression, complete changed-file scope and prior-run
success under the canonical zero-check exception. Never treat a successful single
Actions run as all required checks. A required-workflow ruleset that cannot be
resolved returns ERROR rather than certifying incomplete evidence. Request
failures remain errors; a request reaching its window deadline remains pending.

The helper rediscovers delayed evidence inside each window; it never starts CI.
Use windows at most 540 seconds and shorter than the selected command tool's
supported limit (45 seconds by default). Retain any native command/session ID
when the tool yields. Continue its supported bounded wait to collect completion,
then repeat the helper only on PENDING. Avoid separate status commands, timer
loops, full passing logs, or treating worker turn end as a wakeup.

Read only the selected adapter before invocation. Codex uses `exec_command` and
the returned `session_id` with `write_stdin`; a yielded functions cell uses
`functions.wait` after its cell ID. Claude uses its verified Bash/session
completion API; bounded foreground windows are the sequential fallback.
Antigravity's command/wakeup API is unverified in this repository: map actual
enabled command/wait tools before invocation, otherwise report unavailable.
With an available shell, bounded foreground execution followed by the same
command is the real sequential fallback; do not assume reference reactive APIs.
Mechanical installation tests do not certify native discovery or wakeup.

Evidence lives only in the selected runtime's `tmp/waits/ci/<id>`. No raw GitHub
logs or error output is printed/stored. Inspect only bounded relevant failed
details separately, applying secret handling. Strict mode never invokes `gh`;
use local-verify. Waiting changes no acceptance, TL/QA, or approval-SHA contract.

Selected provider invocation: `--provider claude --runtime-root .claude/agents`. Preserve receipt bindings when customized; load only `.claude/harness/Provider_Adapter.md`.
